10) Denote by /(n) the maximum number of positive integers a l < a 2 < . . . 

not exceeding n for which the sums ai + aj are all different . SIDON asked to estimate /(n). TURIN and I proved that (I. 10 .1) f(n) < ny2 + n'/ ,, and SINGER proved that for infinitely many n (I. 10 .2) f (n) > n% . It is possible that f(n) = ny= + 0(1) .  

> SINGER'S

proof is based on his construction of a perfect difference set i .e . a set of residues a i , a2 , . . . , ak+i (mod n) so that every residue mod n

except 0 can be uniquely represented in the form ai - aj . Clearly a perfect difference set is only possible if n _ k 2 + k + 1 and SINGER proved that a perfect difference set exists if k is a power of a prime . It has been conjectured 15*    

