I proved by probabilistic arguments that such a sequence exists, in fact I proved the existence of a sequence with (1.11 .2) cl log n < g(n) < c 2 log n. 

The existence of a sequence with g(n)/log n = c > 0 is an open problem . An older conjecture of TURÁN and myself stated that if g(n) > 0 for all n > no then lim sup g(n) = - (perhaps even g(n) > c log n for infinitely many n, 

