5) Let aI, a2, . . . , a,, be n elements AI , A2 , . . . , A k , k > 1 sets whose elements are the a's . Assume that each pair (a;, aj) is contained in one and only one A . Then k > n . This is a result of de BRUIJN and myself (also proved by SZEKERES and HANANI) . We can not determine the smallest l so that there should exist sets AI, A 2 , . . . , A,, l > 1 so that every triplet (ai, aj , a,) 

is contained in one and only one A .          

